# A merge-selected body with a control body place, run over the completed result whose layout shifts the selected
# body's slots (as unit_merge_selected_body_shift_call): Later's if body is a place of Later's code graph, reached
# through the code's own index of it -- natively through the result's proved execution map (lmx_implements_code_index),
# in the walker through the root's physical index.  A raw index names Model's cell instead of the if body.  The body
# runs (x = 3), declares t, if\t: 20 writes the place, x reads it back: exit 23.
Model:
    int: x 1
    x: x + 1
    int: y 4
    x: x + 1
end: Model

Later:
    int: pad 2
    int: x 3
    if: x = 3
        int: t 10
    if\t: 20
    x: x + if\t
end: Later

R: merge: Model Later
if: R\x != 3 || R\y != 4 || R\pad != 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
call: R
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: R\x; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
